          RowBox[{"warnings", "=", 
           RowBox[{"{", "\n", "    ", 
            
            RowBox[{"\"\<Only four device J-V plots are generated. No \
power-density plots and no ideal-converter J-V outputs are calculated.\>\"", ",",
              "\n", "    ", "\"\<There is no single intrinsic overall J-V \
curve, Voc or Jsc for unconstrained 3T/4T operation. Two port curves are \
shown. Reference: https://doi.org/10.1021/acsenergylett.0c00068\>\"", ",", 
             "\n", "    ", "\"\<3T scope: two two-terminal subcells in a \
common-Z s-type interconnection with lumped shared resistance. This is not a \
full transport model of an intrinsically three-contact IBC junction. At \
finite Rz, the two port currents are coupled through the shared-lead \
drop.\>\"", ",", "\n", 
             "    ", "\"\<Positive plotted currents deliver power at the \
labeled positive port voltage. The signed outward Z-lead current in \
diagnostics is JSi-JPe; together IT=JPe, IR=-JSi, IZ=JSi-JPe satisfy KCL.\>\"",
              ",", "\n", 
             "    ", "\"\<Series 2T now reaches Vout=0 by continuing existing \
diode/recombination/shunt equations into reverse bias. No avalanche/breakdown \
term is added. The extended segment and extracted Jsc/FF depend on this \
unvalidated reverse-bias assumption; flagged CSV rows identify that \
segment.\>\"", ",", "\n", 
             "    ", "\"\<VMM uses Jlocal=n Jstring. n=1.64 is an effective \
module scaling ratio, not a fractional fabricated Si die.\>\"", ",", "\n", 
             "    ", "\"\<The other EXTERNAL 3T port is held at its joint-MPP \
voltage during each sweep. The displayed states are restricted to the \
intrinsic generating domain. Some finite-Rz curves can therefore stop before \
a zero external voltage endpoint; no extrapolated points are inserted.\>\"", ",",
              "\n", "    ", "\"\<The subcell equations and input parameters \
are inherited from the original notebook. Optical, luminescent, ionic and \
spatial transport effects absent there are not added by this plotting code. \
Numerical consistency is not experimental validation.\>\"", ",", "\n", "    ", 
             RowBox[{"If", "[", 
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{"optics", "==", "\"\<NotebookThin\>\""}], ",", "\n", 
               "      ", "\"\<2T uses the original thin-top generation \
currents; the other architectures use the full-top currents. Select \
SameAsOtherTandems for a common-optics comparison.\>\"", ",", "\n", 
               "      ", "\"\<All architectures use the same full-top \
generation currents.\>\""}], "]"}]}], "}"}]}], ";", "\n", "  ", 
